[{:seon.task/name "a-design-adds-its-proofs"
  :seon.task/plan "Dogfood (the archived paper dogfood-and-docs-2026-10-25.md (git history) gap 1, 3 of 3 agents): a design task made from a staged request has no proofs (```seon.template/stages```: design writes its own), its instructions ask for proofs written as deftests and run red, but ```my.task/update!``` accepts only :seon.task/plan and :seon.task/instructions, and nothing else an agent can call writes :seon.task/proofs. So each deftest the design writes is a :stray-red (```seon.reconcile/not-done```), a reason that carries no :do form (```seon.context/refused```), and no design on a request can be done. The change, at the producer: `update!`'s contract admits :seon.task/proofs, so `(my.task/update! :seon.task/proofs conj 'ns.x-test/a-proof)` adds one on the branch, carried to main at the run's end as plan and instructions already are; the :stray-red reason on a :design task shows that form for its test; the design instructions (`seon.template/instructions` :design) name it. No new attribute."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/a-design-adds-a-proof-with-update seon.context-test/a-stray-red-on-a-design-shows-the-form-that-makes-it-a-proof}}
 {:seon.task/name "status-answers-before-any-turn"
  :seon.task/plan "Dogfood (gap 4): `(my.task/status)`, the form the system prompt names, answers :seon.turn/not-observed until a model turn has observed the task, so an outside agent (Claude through the server) never gets it, and an agent that asks before its first turn's observe gets an error. The observe is a pure measurement of the branch (```seon.turn/observe```). The change: status observes when no turn has (the same measurement a turn makes, recorded as that turn's would be), so it never answers not-observed; delete the not-observed error and its message."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/status-answers-before-any-turn}}]
